{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/248073-major-campaign-arc","id":248073,"title":"Major Campaign Arc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-03T12:24:51-07:00","id":248073,"title":"Major Campaign Arc","content":"Can you share what you're using as the overall &quot;arc&quot; for your Demon campaigns beyond the &quot;Infrastructure of the Week&quot;-style adventures. Most of my player's long-term ambitions are grandiose so I'm not sure I can use them, though I've been making a lot of progress in helping them re-word their ambitions to be more achievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","user":"PencilBoy99","date":". 09-03-2014, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T15:03:29-07:00","id":248159,"title":"","content":"My grand arc, or the whole purpose of this chronicle was to prevent a powerful hunter angel being summoned. But we haven't gotten nearly that far yet. After er 13 games were still in the third story and so far I've only given them the faintest glimpses of that goal. Right now the players are trying to form their own agency so that's been a plot point. They're getting ready to stop a Demon they made an enemy early in game 4 or 5. So saturday they'll be trying to turn his mortal allies against him. Last story they were investigating the God-Machine smelting ghosts and perfect iron to create something huge under in the underworld, but since they're at a loss of where to go we're leaving that in the background for now. Before that in Story one they were dealing with a cryptid infestation.<br /> I've never used an &quot;Infrastructure or Badguy of the week&quot; I have mingling plots that usually take around 5 games to accomplish witch each game being a mix of. Character's personal stuff, Plot A, and some Plot B.<br /> I''m not sure what you mean by Achievable ambitions since honestly I would give my players the chance to do anything they wanted. Whether or not they turn away from that goal later, well that's just half the fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T15:57:07-07:00","id":248202,"title":"","content":"Funny. I just meant that they had to come up with something they wanted to work on and actually did stuff towards. They're still learning how to get beats and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T16:40:23-07:00","id":248236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/248073-major-campaign-arc?p=248159#post248159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My grand arc, or the whole purpose of this chronicle was to prevent a powerful hunter angel being summoned. But we haven't gotten nearly that far yet. After er 13 games were still in the third story and so far I've only given them the faintest glimpses of that goal. Right now the players are trying to form their own agency so that's been a plot point. They're getting ready to stop a Demon they made an enemy early in game 4 or 5. So saturday they'll be trying to turn his mortal allies against him. Last story they were investigating the God-Machine smelting ghosts and perfect iron to create something huge under in the underworld, but since they're at a loss of where to go we're leaving that in the background for now. Before that in Story one they were dealing with a cryptid infestation.<br /> I've never used an &quot;Infrastructure or Badguy of the week&quot; I have mingling plots that usually take around 5 games to accomplish witch each game being a mix of. Character's personal stuff, Plot A, and some Plot B.<br /> I''m not sure what you mean by Achievable ambitions since honestly I would give my players the chance to do anything they wanted. Whether or not they turn away from that goal later, well that's just half the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example of your Plot A versus your Plot B in a given session? I think what you're doing is my ideal, I just haven't been able to figure out how to do that in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T18:47:42-07:00","id":248353,"title":"","content":"Sure let's go with what's going on right now. Last story an Angel named Themnos helped the characters with a task non-GM related that they were working on. In exchange they did something for him that didn't make much sense to them (Of course it wouldn't). This was the start of the main plot for Story three but took place in Story two. So it was just a little blurb in one game with some little stuff through the rest of the story this was last story's B while Plot A was them investigating an unrelated Infrastructure. Now In story three with Story Two's A as complete as we'll get for now. Two's B became Three's A and within the next game (Story three game 2) we added Story Three's B plot. B's only take about a scene. . <br /> Here's a chart.<br /> Story One<br /> A, A, A, A, AB.<br /> Story Two. (Where A is the previous B)<br /> A, A, A, AB, AB.<br /> Story Three<br /> A, A, AB, AB, AB<br /> So chapter Four will go<br /> A, AB, AB, AB, AB. <br /> <br /> And this will continue until every game is two plots and then I'll be using a different set up. This mind is on top of each character's personal stuff going on. Whether it be Cover related or just Demon related that the other players don't need to be or don't want to be involved with. <br /> <br /> Since my players are becoming stronger and more accomplished plus we're all getting better with the system I feel and they've shown that they can handle the excess plot. It's also great because if I get stumped on something or they blow me away with something clever, or anything else we have a fall back avenue to pursue.<br /> <br /> I'm -really- sorry if that was too drawn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:29:03-07:00","id":248883,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The overall plot of the chronicle I'm running now is basically that an Angel that specializes in creating stigmatic Sleeper Agents has been inactive for about 18 years. There is a new Project on the horizon and the God-Machine needs a specialist group of Stigmatics that can be plucked from their life for various purposes. The special way this angel brainwashes people though is more akin to a spreadable disease. The more the subject is aware of the Angel and the more the subject thinks on the enigma that it causes the more the sickness grows. When the sickness grows strong enough the subject can be completely controlled when the Angel's presence is near. The are then given a Mask that emulates the Angel's presence. <br /> <br /> The sickness spreads by the subject involving those they know in their &quot;pursuit of answers&quot; or by wearing the masks and targeting others when the Angel chooses the stigmatic to do so. Because this &quot;sickness&quot; grows and spreads faster among children they are usually targets. However it has been 18 years and almost everyone from the original kindergarten class was made as a sleeper except one of the Player's Covers that only escaped this fate by moving away during the year. Now the Angel wants to complete the set and is targeting these other people that the cover associates with.<br /> <br /> The Angel has no idea that it is targeting Demons and the Demons are freaked the hell out that they seem to be targeted through nothing that they did </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Of course we are still only in the first story so none of that has really come up. All they know is a couple people with powerful masks were looking at 2 of the characters and that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:33:40-07:00","id":248887,"title":"","content":"I want to be miss_mintty when I grow up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:51:19-07:00","id":248924,"title":"","content":"I think we all do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T15:08:56-07:00","id":249196,"title":"","content":"My chronicle arc is based around an antagonist angel known as &quot;The Inevitable&quot;.<br /> <br /> It begins with a mysterious Facility that is built beneath Seattle University and accessible by a building that no human can see on the campus grounds, known as &quot;The Beachhead&quot;. The Facility's primary function was to interrogate and detail &quot;Hell&quot; using a demon known as Linchpin. The God-Machine appears to have made a terrible mistake, however, in that It assigned a Messenger angel to interrogate and learn everything about Hell from the captured demon (Linchpin). This inevitably resulted in that angel's fall. This is turn caused other problems as the realisation of choice sank in for other angels working in the Facility, a psychopomp whom was tasked with creating the horrible angelic servitors known as Dalga decided that she did not want to kill to create, but to create properly and nurture the young. She soon fell.<br /> <br /> As the Facility collapsed a new angel was activated at the heart of the Facility, known as &quot;The Inevitable&quot;, and looking like death-warmed-up, this very powerful Destroyer is tasked with &quot;cleaning up&quot; the Facility's broken parts before self-destructing the structure. It seemed the God-Machine wasn't without a contingency plan.<br /> <br /> As a Rank 4 angel at the beginning of the game that is constantly hunting the ring <i>in addition</i> to any hunters they might bring down on their heads through compromise rolls I gave the Inevitable his own condition. The idea being that, as his mission is specifically to clean up the messes of the Facility, he isn't listening in on high-wave angel radio for any possible demon-sightings. Instead he is listening for very specific tells which they may not always show when they make mistakes.<br /> <br /> The main story is therefore, a series of stories, including them finding and rescuing the Linchpin to earn a new ally (they did this) and to defeat the Inevitable and/or subvert the Beachhead. Through doing these things they will learn the truth behind the Beachhead and why the God-Machine appears to have made such a simple mistake.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#4c4c4c\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The Inevitable (Persistent)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The Reloaded Ring is hunted by a Destroyer known as \u201cThe Inevitable\u201d. This angel's mission is solely to destroy the former angels of the Beachhead Facility hidden in Seattle University. The Inevitable may roll (10 \u2013 Cover) dice once per chapter or day (whichever comes first) and must accrue (Cover) successes, when he does this he may appear in a scene and attempt to destroy the ring. If he manages to gain a general profile of any demon's Cover, he gains a +1 to this roll. If he knows their identity he can now harass them regularly and thus gains a +2 (in addition the demon gains the Blown persistent condition). The storyteller may also then in either case have this condition trigger instead of the Surveilled or Hunted (Persistent) conditions as the Inevitable learns to interpret the unique signatures a demon leaves behind when they've been compromised.<br /> <span style=\"color:#4c4c4c\"><b>Resolution:</b></span> The Inevitable must die to resolve this condition. In order to remove his +2 bonus upon him identifying a Demon's cover, the demon must abandon that cover.<br /> <span style=\"color:#4c4c4c\"><b>Beat:</b></span> Any time the Inevitable enters a scene, the involved demons gain a beat. Any time the ring escape or kill the Inevitable they gain a beat.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 09-04-2014, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:08:36-07:00","id":249266,"title":"","content":"Desolate Dolly, I might take fragments of that facility for my game if you don't mind? One of the player's character's covers goes to school there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T00:11:52-07:00","id":249601,"title":"","content":"I've got a project in the works right now that revolves around a serial killer going around Seattle killing seemingly random Stigmatics and Demons. The whole premise of the Chronicle is a play on movies where a high tech-intelligence agency has to track down and stop a dangerous serial killer that seems to always be one step ahead of them, with the high-tech intelligence agency being Seattle's Demon Agencies and the dangerous serial killer being an obviously supernatural but none the less unknown serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T03:49:05-07:00","id":249675,"title":"","content":"My major campaing arc is about the Iraq war. My players can remember things about a mission they've done in there when they were still angels of the machine: God-machine was protecting something vital against an enemy's attack, and now they know it's a code that can be translated into a map of the most vital Infrastructures around the world.<br /> Well, if the enemy could get acess to this code, it could lead to the destruction of the God-machine or the reality. They failed. <br /> <br /> But now the players are the enemies. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T08:00:14-07:00","id":249819,"title":"","content":"miss_minty, need another player?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T14:50:25-07:00","id":250147,"title":"","content":"Do you live in or around Coeur D alene Idaho? My game is all in person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T21:56:51-07:00","id":250487,"title":"","content":"My plans are still very much in the formative stages. I don't like to set too much into motion until I have a sloid understanding of the types of characters that will be in play. Right now the plan is to set my game primarily in the Midtown area of Detroit which has historic ties to the Freemasons. It's an area steeped in history that has fallen on hard times, but is now on the upswing. The general idea is that Detroit was once heavily under the sway of the God Machine, but with concerted effort became something of a way station for the Unchained who managed the city poorly. Recently the God Machine and his angelic agents have made inroads in the Midtown area, and are attempting to seize control for reasons.<br /> <br /> I really want to focus on Free Masons, who are part of a cult of stigmatics attempting to influence the actions of the God Machine, but can alternatively fall under the sway of both Demons and Angels. I also plan to contrast the old Detroit of the 1920s which is still very much alive in Midtown with the newer more vibrant Detroit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/737-campbell","name":"Campbell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T15:36:17-07:00","id":251095,"title":"","content":"After listening to the No Soul Left Behind Actual Play podcast on Role Playing Public Radio, I want to adapt that general idea to Demon. Start with the premise that the PCs are all Demons who had some connection to a school and Fell together, and see where it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T15:48:36-07:00","id":251102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/248073-major-campaign-arc?p=249266#post249266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Desolate Dolly, I might take fragments of that facility for my game if you don't mind? One of the player's character's covers goes to school there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T17:35:41-07:00","id":256381,"title":"","content":"I've found a larger epic arc for a campaign is best when it's broken in a series of smaller sessions. Sort of like what x-files did with its &quot;monster of the week&quot; shows, but with a larger mystery/idea that unveils there's something deeper that everything links to.<br /> <br /> Demon games, I feel, should feel like that onion of conspiracies; and with more layers being peeled back, more mysteries should be revealed and ever session just helps go down the rabbit hole further.<br /> <br /> Without copy-and-pasted the 10 page outline I have, the main underlying mystery involves the real-world mystery of number stations:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numbers_station\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numbers_station\" target=\"_blank\"> Numbers station - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numbers_station\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numbers_station </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's an example of the broadcast. Tell me that doesn't sound creepy and God-Machine-ish!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=McFRonD-sjg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=McFRonD-sjg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=McFRonD-sjg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=McFRonD-sjg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, as all the smaller campaigns progress and get resolved, more mysteries are uncovered and more questions get asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T21:19:06-07:00","id":256464,"title":"","content":"In the beginning...<br /> <br /> The ring was contacted by a patron who them to explore and record the infrastructure of a new a city.<br /> <br /> After playing &quot;How an angel dies&quot; (adapted for the new location) They set themselves up with Pacts to adapt existing Covers (other players played the hapless mortal NPCs during negotiation, one character managed to secure a Soul pact) and the first mission the players subvert an Infrastructure which is being used as a home base, or at least as a common source of Aether and Gadget making.<br /> <br /> The thrust of the campaign is that the city opens out in Splinters, but in this city they lead to potential <i>futures</i>, not alternate pasts. The players are currently exploring one based on Infinite Macabre. I'm grafting two of the Shards in he Storytellers guide onto the two I have so far. The players are investigating these Splinters for variet <br /> <br /> Future adventure set pieces include:<ul><li>An angelic cult that equips itself with Form Gadgets created from demons that they capture and vivisect</li> <li>Interacting with the VASCU regional headquarters operating within the main timeline.</li> <li>The SOE finding itself into the main timeline and the players have to fight them for control of Infrastructure that connects Splinters</li> <li>Industrial espionage operating between Deva Corporation and rival megacorporations</li> <li>Exploring the 3 remaining Splinters</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/248073-major-campaign-arc?p=256381#post256381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without copy-and-pasted the 10 page outline I have, the main underlying mystery involves the real-world mystery of number stations:</div> </div> </div> </div>Darth, have you listened to the 99% Invisible podcast on that very subject? <i>Highly</i> recommended if you have not already","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T23:47:43-07:00","id":256546,"title":"","content":"I haven't completely figure out what I will do yet, but it will surely involve Lake Waiau, on Maunakea here in Hawaii. I recently learnt that this lake is, like the whole mountain sacred to Hawaiians. Its particularity? Mothers (used to) bring the umbilical cords of their babies to the lake after giving birth ...<br /> Gross? Yes.<br /> Now, as you may know, on top of Maunakea, there are some of the best astronomical observatories (i.e. giant telescopes) in the world ... so buildings filled with wheels, electronics, bolts, ... everything an Infrastructure of the God-Machine usually has.<br /> On top of that, and as I said before, the mountain is sacred to native Hawaiians, and there is, from time to time, protests about the use of the mountain by astronomers.<br /> <br /> As one of them (astronomers, not protesters), I thought it could be interesting to have the telescopes and the top of the mountain corrupted by Infrastructures, the lake (and the mothers bringing placental matter there) being part of an occult matrix, and the protesters being lead by some Demons or at least some anti God-Machine group.<br /> My only player (my wife) is also an astronomer, therefore I will play on the counter-intuitiveness of the situation.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure yet about the goal of the Infrastructure, as I'm focusing on how to lead the Demons to Hawaii first.<br /> Again, I want to play the counter-intuitive card to my wife: I thought I would start with a Planned Parenthood office hiding an Infrastructure where the God-Machine is collecting foetuses and placental matter for 2 occult matrices. One of them is the Hawaiian one, but I will make it look secondary. The collecting of foetuses should be more shocking and will put the Demon on another path for some time.<br /> <br /> Not much so far, just a couple of pieces that I need to tie together in a bigger story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1841-nflagey","name":"nflagey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T01:54:34-07:00","id":256578,"title":"","content":"Grand arch plan: GM is really the jailer of the titans and when the demons sabotage a piece of infrastructure with security like no other they have ever seen a (weakened) titan wakes....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T14:05:25-07:00","id":256815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/248073-major-campaign-arc?p=256464#post256464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the beginning...<br /> Darth, have you listened to the 99% Invisible podcast on that very subject? <i>Highly</i> recommended if you have not already</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I've never heard of that podcast, but I'll have to check it out. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}